{
  "title": "Which producer a call reaches (carrick-match pair_winners)",
  "version": 1,
  "contract": "carrick-tools/carrick#3496; implemented by carrick-match pair_winners (native + wasm) and run byte-identical by carrick-cloud lambdas/mcp-server (parity test). A change to this file is a contract change: change both copies and re-pin both sha256 values together.",
  "rule": [
    "Inputs are canonical keys as stored: producer full_path, consumer canonical path. The function never rewrites them (see canonical_path for the write-side form).",
    "Non-HTTP (graphql, socket, pubsub): a producer pairs when protocol, name and (socket) direction are equal and names_pair(call, producer) holds. Every such producer is a winner. No ranking.",
    "HTTP, in order: (1) a call path with no literal segment is unknown_call_path and pairs with nothing; (2) the pool is every HTTP producer, in every service including the caller's own, whose method serves the call's (method_matches: case-insensitive, producer ALL serves every method, consumer ALL only producer ALL); (3) producers whose path routes the call (match_agreement is defined) are ranked by agreement and only the maximal ones are kept, ties kept; nothing routes -> no_route; (4) each kept producer answers match_verdict_with_dispatch; (5) dispatch_outcome over those answers decides: matched -> winners are the matched producers; route_case_unknown -> winners are the dispatching producers whose case the call does not state (one edge to the route, case unknown); no_case_answers -> no winner; otherwise (best agreement 0: a bare catch-all or a param-only route) -> no_literal_agreement, no winner.",
    "Every winner carries same_service (producer service == call service), relationship (producer_consumer for route-definition evidence, shared_external_contract for call-site evidence) and, for HTTP, call_param_over_route_literal (the call has a placeholder where this route states a literal: carrick#2004; the edge stands, the type check does not compare). These are facts, not filters: what a surface draws for them is its documented policy.",
    "routed lists every maximal-agreement producer with its verdict, for reasons and near-miss text. It is empty for non-HTTP calls, unknown_call_path and no_route.",
    "A case carrying expected_red pins today's answer for a product gap the case names: the answer is right for this function's rule and wrong for the product. Its expect is checked like any other; the marker says what turns the product green and must be removed by the change that does."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "all-route-serves-post-call",
      "source": "probe cloud_vs_scanner.cjs case 1; carrick-cloud#962",
      "input": {
        "producers": [
          {
            "service": "api",
            "protocol": "http",
            "method": "ALL",
            "path": "/graphql"
          }
        ],
        "call": {
          "service": "web",
          "protocol": "http",
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/graphql"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "outcome": "matched",
        "winners": [
          {
            "producer": 0,
            "verdict": "matched",
            "agreement": 1,
            "same_service": false,
            "relationship": "producer_consumer",
            "call_param_over_route_literal": false
          }
        ],
        "routed": [
          {
            "producer": 0,
            "verdict": "matched",
            "agreement": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    },
