      "id": "trailing-slash-route-is-not-canonical",
      "source": "rust_probe.out row 5; audit I5. Stays no_route: the route-side writer owes canonical_path (address chain join), pairing does not rewrite stored keys",
      "expected_red": "Wanted: matched. A trailing slash on a stored route key is a writer's mistake: the route-side writers owe canonical_path (carrick#3496 follow-up F1, with the address chain join). pair_winners never rewrites its inputs, so this case answers no_route until the stored key is canonical.",
      "input": {
        "producers": [
          {
            "service": "api",
            "protocol": "http",
            "method": "GET",
            "path": "/api/users/"
          }
        ],
        "call": {
          "service": "web",
          "protocol": "http",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/api/users"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "outcome": "no_route",
        "winners": [],
        "routed": []
